ckend services, LLM-powered applications, in-house models, web extensions, and API development to support real-time and post-call operations.\nAs the organization expands, we are adding a Junior AI Engineer to support new AI projects, model development, backend engineering, and cloud-based services. This role offers the opportunity to learn from highly experienced engineers, work in an Agile environment, and contribute to next-generation agent-assist capabilities.\nWhat You’ll Do Contribute to AI-driven projects within the C3 Space, supporting agent-focused applications including call summaries, AgentAssist tools, and AI-driven extensions.Collaborate with senior engineers on Python-based development, including multithreading, backend logic, and model-driven workflows.Assist in developing, maintaining, and optimizing in-house AI/ML models, alongside large language model (LLM) integrations.Support web-based initiatives including front-end extensions, internal tools, browser-based (Wixy) interfaces, and supporting APIs.Participate in backend development using modern engineering practices to support Strata and other contact-center platforms.Work with cloud-based infrastructure across any major cloud provider (AWS, Azure, or GCP).Contribute to Agile ceremonies and collaborate closely with engineers across multiple squads as the team scales into two dedicated groups.Learn, iterate, and quickly ramp up on new tools, languages, and AI frameworks within a supportive, growth-oriented environment.\nRequired Skills & Qualifications Programming: Strong proficiency in Python (must-have).Additional Languages: Exposure to or experience with JavaScript/TypeScript.AI/ML Interest: Academic, personal, or project-based experience in AI, ML, generative AI, or data science.Backend Foundations: Understanding of backend development concepts; hands-on experience building backend systems is a strong plus.Cloud Knowledge: Familiarity with at least one cloud platform (AWS, Azure, or GCP).API Fu